/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( A requirement for the 48-volt system is voltage changes needed to happen on the bottom side. The electrical team worked to ensure majority of all electronics were housed in the canister of Nomad. The cylindrical acrylic enclosure ensured all electronics were safe guarded against leaks and accessible for any alternations. The enclosure, also referred to as canister, is sealed off using two enclosure caps, one with a clear acrylic face for the camera to see out of, and one with holes for wires and cables to run to from the enclosure \(Fig 9\). )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
