288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (     To connect the top and bottom sides for our product, we used a 23-meter-long tether that contains our ethernet cord, power cable, and high-pressure resistant tubing. This is then collected together in an expandable mesh cover with a high dense buoyancy foam tubing inside it to keep the tether buoyant \(Fig 10\). The tether is then managed by one or two people on deck to be certain that the tether is not kinking and to pull back or give away any slack that the pilot needs for the needs or does not need.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
