339 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The first challenge was scheduling with the team. Because we are from a community college, most students have other obligations such as work to find a time to meet up. The team has been using Discord to communicate with each other to get the most interaction possible. Another challenge was ordering parts for the ROV. This was a complex bureaucratic process that required approval from more than three people.  Delays happened because we could not get the parts when we expected. Similarly, retention and recruitment was difficult. As a small community college, recruiting more members was a challenge because the students are usually too busy with other commitments; also most students are transferring out of community college to a higher university in a two year time so the team that we have will not be as experienced as a four year institution.  An obvious challenge was when testing at the pool and our electronics were overheating. There is not much shade at the pool but we used towels to shade our equipment. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
